      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-69",
        "notes": "Proof 1.1–2.1 reviewed against the path definition, mean value theorem, dominated convergence and L1 linearity. A compact rectangular neighborhood supplies coordinate segments and one integrable bound. Difference quotients are dominated; derivatives are measurable limits, and C1 conditional regularity plus domination gives continuity of their integrals. Finite sums commute with the integral. Strict positivity and finite local integrals justify J/p; only interior time is claimed. No endpoint derivative or result at p=0 is asserted. No reader/refuter finding or defect."
      }
