      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-69",
        "notes": "Proof 1.1–2.1 and all eleven cited supplier interfaces reviewed. Q has mass one by Tonelli, even with time-dependent exceptional endpoint sets. Finite LM and C make the cross term L1 by the two Cauchy–Schwarz inequalities; Fubini cancels its endpoint mean. Thus LC=LM+C with C nonnegative and theta-independent. The reader difference-of-squares identity derives the same correct derivative directly from bilinearity. Compact parameter balls and fixed-null-set derivative envelopes justify difference quotients and continuous derivatives by MVT/DCT. Bounded fields give integrable envelopes because Q and its marginal have mass one. PDE conclusion uses the already reviewed local-domination lemma. No false claim found in either hash-bound version: the derivative expansion is audit enrichment of an immediate elementary calculation."
      }
