        "notes": "All four verification steps and ten supplier interfaces reviewed. Finite endpoint support supplies local compact derivative bounds and pi-integrability; Gaussian positivity makes the quotient finite and positive. Density ratio is exp(2atx/sigma²); weighted endpoint mean is a tanh(atx/sigma²), and 1-tc=1/sigma gives the stated velocity. For t>0,a>0, k,beta>0, tanh(2y)<2tanh(y) for y>0 rules out affine linearity. t=0 is correctly excluded; sigma_min=1 remains nonlinear at t>0. Reader correction of F6 accurately separates the power-series definition from positivity/reciprocal and addition suppliers and derives exp(0)=1. This is a completed nonfatal citation-attribution repair; mathematics and interface unchanged."
