        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-69",
        "notes": "Proof 1.1–3.1 and all fifteen direct suppliers reviewed. Finite losses at each visited iterate extend to a compact parameter box by coordinatewise MVT and the local derivative envelopes; the gradient theorem then applies to that restricted open domain. The reader bilinear difference quotient is a sound explicit derivation of the elementary sample-gradient formula. Joint measurability/Tonelli define m(theta); fresh-batch independence, explicit random-iterate integrability and Fubini establish its integrability and eventwise conditional-expectation identity, without assuming a globally integrable random envelope. B>=1 permits averaging; zero step sizes remain valid and staying in Theta is assumed. Smooth global-flow supplier is read through its full proof and used with T=1 and precisely its open-time-domain, compact-parameter Lipschitz/origin bounds. Joint continuity makes the random-parameter terminal output measurable; independent X0 gives the asserted conditional pushforward. N=0 has no gradient obligation and retains the flow conclusion. No target-law equality or numerical/convergence/complexity guarantee is claimed. No defect found; reader expansion is audit enrichment."
